00:42:05,190 --> 00:42:07,025
To try and find the cows.

996
00:42:07,058 --> 00:42:09,828
When he came back again,
he was quite crazy.

997
00:42:09,862 --> 00:42:11,763
And he says that the whole thing
is your fault.

998
00:42:11,797 --> 00:42:14,400
- That's nonsense!
- We haven't touched the cows!

999
00:42:14,433 --> 00:42:16,235
--Since you arrived.

1000
00:42:16,268 --> 00:42:17,837
First of all,
we had the volcanoes.

1001
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,505
Then we had the monsters.

1002
00:42:19,538 --> 00:42:21,840
And all since you arrived.

1003
00:42:21,873 --> 00:42:23,475
Now. Get out!

1004
00:42:23,508 --> 00:42:25,643
- [Bots strain]
- Hey! Hey!

1005
00:42:25,677 --> 00:42:27,045
Everybody in
the village there!

1006
00:42:27,078 --> 00:42:28,880
Every farmer
who's lost a cow!

1007
00:42:28,913 --> 00:42:32,652
Hey, mrs. O'leary's cow
tipped over the lantern.

1008
00:42:32,685 --> 00:42:34,387
Come on! Call the men in!

1009
00:42:34,420 --> 00:42:36,688
We need more skin bracer!

1010
00:42:36,722 --> 00:42:38,557
Menin.

1011
00:42:38,590 --> 00:42:41,227
Let's just forget the milk.

1012
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:44,028
Must you take that
with you everywhere?

1013
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:45,932
- Huh?
- Oh, it's-- oh.

1014
00:42:45,965 --> 00:42:48,600
Mom, if the u.N. Calls,
I'm playing with my slot car.

1015
00:42:48,633 --> 00:42:50,168
Put your toys away.

1016
00:42:50,202 --> 00:42:51,937
Don't you touch them.

1017
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:53,305
They're part of the set.

1018
00:42:53,338 --> 00:42:54,707
Now I can't do
the next scene.

1019
00:42:54,740 --> 00:42:56,408
Whoo-hoo!

1020
00:42:56,442 --> 00:42:58,310
Eiichi, not so loud.

1021
00:42:58,343 --> 00:42:59,578
You'll disturb granddad.

1022
00:42:59,612 --> 00:43:02,915
Granddad's
already disturbed.

1023
00:43:02,948 --> 00:43:05,417
They've been in there
for more than three hours now.

1024
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:06,685
Just saying the same things
over and over.

1025
00:43:06,718 --> 00:43:08,853
I swear, this is
the last blanket I'm washing.

1026
00:43:08,887 --> 00:43:12,190
--Getting nowhere.

1027
00:43:12,223 --> 00:43:15,693
So you think
we ought to wait a while?

1028
00:43:15,727 --> 00:43:17,462
Yes, I do.

1029
00:43:17,495 --> 00:43:19,998
Well, you know what they say
about animals running away.

1030
00:43:20,032 --> 00:43:23,168
- [All cackle]
- --A disaster is coming.

1031
00:43:23,202 --> 00:43:24,837
Don't you think
we'd be better off

1032
00:43:24,870 --> 00:43:27,572
selling the land now,
while we can?

1033
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,708
I'm an old man,
but we've never had

1034
00:43:29,742 --> 00:43:31,343
any troubles
like this before.

1035
00:43:31,377 --> 00:43:32,712
Not ever since
I can remember.

1036
00:43:32,745 --> 00:43:33,978
- Which is last wednesday.
- I know that we'll

1037
00:43:34,012 --> 00:43:35,880
lose some money.
But I'm still not sure

1038
00:43:35,913 --> 00:43:37,448
we wouldn't be
a lot better off if we took

1039
00:43:37,482 --> 00:43:39,718
the company's present offer
for the land and got out?

1040
00:43:39,752 --> 00:43:42,520
What about that hired gun
named shane?

1041
00:43:42,553 --> 00:43:44,790
Yes, you're right.
I can't get to sleep at night

1042
00:43:44,823 --> 00:43:46,292
for worrying about it.

1043
00:43:46,325 --> 00:43:47,927
Just waiting
for it to come out.

1044
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,795
It's stupid of you
to take this attitude.

1045
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:51,963
- Dig.
- If they know
you're weakening,

1046
00:43:51,997 --> 00:43:54,867
well then, they'll just
drive the price even lower.

1047
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:56,302
Wilford brimley?

1048
00:43:56,335 --> 00:43:58,837
- No.
- You want to get more money,
don't you?

1049
00:43:58,870 --> 00:44:01,440
You want to let the land go
for any less than it's worth?

1050
00:44:01,473 --> 00:44:02,173
Do you?

1051
00:44:02,207 --> 00:44:04,275
Of course we don't.

1052
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:06,278
It's the right thing to do.

1053
00:44:06,312 --> 00:44:08,280
So then, trust me.

1054
00:44:08,313 --> 00:44:10,782
Just let me handle
the negotiations for you.

1055
00:44:10,815 --> 00:44:13,418
Do you really think we can get
california for us all?

1056
00:44:15,687 --> 00:44:17,555
Here's the news.
The monster gaos is causing

1057
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:19,290
great damage
to the mountain provinces.

1058
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,727
Up to now, none of the police
nor the armed services--

1059
00:44:21,760 --> 00:44:24,262
- hmm?
- Hey, those helmets
are multiplying.

1060
00:44:24,295 --> 00:44:25,797
- Oh.
- --Going to report the number
of people are missing.

1061
00:44:25,830 --> 00:44:27,665
[Man shouts]

1062
00:44:27,700 --> 00:44:29,435
What?

1063
00:44:29,468 --> 00:44:31,303
Turn down the radio!

1064
00:44:31,337 --> 00:44:33,205
--And police authorities.

1065
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:36,942
Aah! More helmets.

1066
00:44:36,975 --> 00:44:38,210
You're leaving
your jobs now?

1067
00:44:38,243 --> 00:44:39,645
Yes. May as well.

1068
00:44:39,678 --> 00:44:41,747
There's nothing for us
to do here now.

1069
00:44:41,780 --> 00:44:43,648
Work on the road stopped
altogether.

1070
00:44:43,682 --> 00:44:45,650
And we're worried about
this monster, too.

1071
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,787
Hey, looks like
il duce up there.

1072
00:44:47,820 --> 00:44:49,220
- The big benito?
- Mm-hmm.

1073
00:44:49,253 --> 00:44:50,788
Well, I'm sorry
to see you going.

1074
00:44:50,822 --> 00:44:53,258
- Hope you find work.
- Don't forget to call us

1075
00:44:53,292 --> 00:44:55,260
when the work stops again,
will you, boss?

1076
00:44:55,293 --> 00:44:57,028
- Oh, sure.
- Yeah, right.

1077
00:44:57,062 --> 00:44:58,563
Right. Let's go.

1078
00:44:58,597 --> 00:45:00,698
All right. If we get work.

1079
00:45:00,732 --> 00:45:03,135
Get moving now.
See you guys.

1080
00:45:05,970 --> 00:45:08,507
Hey, where's my helmet?

1081
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:12,410
How long do you think we're
gonna have to stay up here?

1082
00:45:12,443 --> 00:45:14,378
I'll stay as long as
I'm in charge.

1083
00:45:14,413 --> 00:45:16,282
You're in charge
of nothing, pal.

1084
00:45:16,315 --> 00:45:18,117
--I'm gonna have to stay.

1085
00:45:18,150 --> 00:45:20,418
Hey look, he's got
a pac-man jacket.

1086
00:45:20,452 --> 00:45:21,853
Do you two
want to move out now?

1087
00:45:21,887 --> 00:45:23,522
Of course not.

1088
00:45:23,555 --> 00:45:24,990
Neither of us is afraid
of the monster,

1089
00:45:25,023 --> 00:45:26,492
so why should we leave?

1090
00:45:26,525 --> 00:45:29,127
[All imitate curly]

1091
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:31,097
He doesn't worry us at all.

1092
00:45:31,130 --> 00:45:32,765
[All chuckle]

1093
00:45:36,602 --> 00:45:38,270
Is he the catcher
in the rye?

1094
00:45:38,303 --> 00:45:41,307
- Sheesh.
- --You, scaring us like that?

1095
00:45:41,340 --> 00:45:43,208
- "Scaring us like that?"
- There's nothing
to be scared of.

1096
00:45:43,242 --> 00:45:44,843
Why do you say that?

1097
00:45:44,877 --> 00:45:47,145
Gaos is a very
ferocious monster.

1098
00:45:47,178 --> 00:45:48,547
You mean you ain't scared?

1099
00:45:48,580 --> 00:45:50,548
Not at daytime. You see,

1100
00:45:50,582 --> 00:45:52,017
he only comes out
in the night time.

1101
00:45:52,050 --> 00:45:54,820
I thank the lord
for the night time.

1102
00:45:54,853 --> 00:45:57,155
Tell us
how you found that out.

1103
00:45:57,188 --> 00:45:58,790
I wrote it down in my diary.

1104
00:45:58,823 --> 00:46:00,725
When gaos comes out,
I just write down the time.

1105
00:46:00,758 --> 00:46:02,327
Usually right after cheers.

1106
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:04,630
- Mm.
- Oh, I see.

1107
00:46:04,663 --> 00:46:06,232
Mitch miller?

1108
00:46:06,265 --> 00:46:07,867
It never occurred
to any of us that gaos

1109
00:46:07,900 --> 00:46:10,068
might be
a nocturnal beast.

1110
00:46:10,102 --> 00:46:11,937
Hiding out during
the daytime,

1111
00:46:11,970 --> 00:46:13,272
and coming out at night.

1112
00:46:13,305 --> 00:46:15,007
That's right. We never saw even
a glimpse of him

1113
00:46:15,040 --> 00:46:16,375
during the bombing attack.

1114
00:46:16,408 --> 00:46:18,543
He kept right undercover
the whole time.

1115
00:46:18,577 --> 00:46:21,112
In that case, we need only
watch for him at night.

1116
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:23,615
And you can call off your troops
during the daytime, then.

1117
00:46:23,648 --> 00:46:26,050
Commander. Don't you have some
special new flares that're

1118
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:28,053
supposed to be practically
as light as daylight?

1119
00:46:28,087 --> 00:46:29,453
Yes, we've been
developing some

1120
00:46:29,488 --> 00:46:30,922
specially for
anti-guerilla warfare

1121
00:46:30,955 --> 00:46:32,590
known as the a.G.I.L.
Flare system.

1122
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:35,393
- ...thing.
- However, they are still
in the trial stage.

1123
00:46:35,427 --> 00:46:36,862
Oh, we gotta go.

1124
00:46:36,895 --> 00:46:38,130
- Okay.
- Let's try them.

1125
00:46:38,163 --> 00:46:39,765
It seems that gaos
is sensitive to light.

1126
00:46:39,798 --> 00:46:41,633
- Thanks, dad.
- And if it does seem
that he has

1127
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:44,468
any particular weaknesses,
we must be sure to exploit them.

1128
00:46:51,643 --> 00:46:55,280
Okay, now listen, tom.
This is the deus ex machina

1129
00:46:55,313 --> 00:46:56,982
which is the god machine.

1130
00:46:57,015 --> 00:47:00,318
Okay? In case we can't think of
any way to end the play,

1131
00:47:00,352 --> 00:47:02,053
- I'm gonna
lower you down, okay?
- Okay.

1132
00:47:02,087 --> 00:47:03,622
And have a big production
ending, all right?

1133
00:47:03,655 --> 00:47:05,757
- Roger.
- I can't get into this, joel.

1134
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:07,192
"Ich bin ein monster?"

1135
00:47:07,225 --> 00:47:08,493
- What's that
supposed to mean?
- All right.

1136
00:47:08,527 --> 00:47:10,428
I just need you
to fake it, okay?

1137
00:47:10,462 --> 00:47:12,430
Uh, let's have those
footlights, cambot.

1138
00:47:12,463 --> 00:47:15,600
- Ooh.
- Um, welcome
to our production,

1139
00:47:15,633 --> 00:47:18,770
which is a combination
of the gotterdammerung

1140
00:47:18,803 --> 00:47:21,473
and gamera vs. Gaos.

1141
00:47:21,507 --> 00:47:25,277
We call it
the gamera-damera.

1142
00:47:25,310 --> 00:47:28,113
Okay? Okay, spuds,
let's really get working now.

1143
00:47:28,147 --> 00:47:29,480
Here we go.

1144
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:32,450
♪♪ [Bots fake-trumpet]

1145
00:47:32,483 --> 00:47:33,885
Mein...

1146
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:37,322
- Mein lieber schatz--
- oh, we got movie sign!

1147
00:47:37,355 --> 00:47:40,792
[Servo groans]

1148
00:47:47,498 --> 00:47:49,067
Ouch, that hurt.

1149
00:47:49,100 --> 00:47:50,635
Oh boy, that hurt.

1150
00:47:50,668 --> 00:47:53,338
Oh. Take that stuff out.

1151
00:47:53,372 --> 00:47:56,107
- What a jip.
- Hey.

1152
00:47:56,140 --> 00:47:57,977
A thousand points-- I'm gonna
give you the third degree!

1153
00:47:58,010 --> 00:47:59,912
- Answer!
- You know what burns my butt?

1154
00:47:59,945 --> 00:48:01,547
A flame about that high.

1155
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:03,448
- [Servo chuckles]
- You fool!

1156
00:48:03,482 --> 00:48:07,085
I-- I just happen
to be cold, that's all.

1157
00:48:07,118 --> 00:48:09,053
You could've fooled me.

1158
00:48:09,087 --> 00:48:11,022
[Explosion]

1159
00:48:11,055 --> 00:48:12,457
- Aah! It's coming!
- It's coming!

1160
00:48:12,490 --> 00:48:16,295
- Aah! Ricky! Aah!
- Take it easy.

1161
00:48:16,328 --> 00:48:18,263
There's nothing
to worry about now.

1162
00:48:18,297 --> 00:48:19,765
Not with the new flares.

1163
00:48:19,798 --> 00:48:21,933
Each one of them's more than
six million candle power.

1164
00:48:21,967 --> 00:48:24,670
That's four times brighter
than the moon, when at maximum.

1165
00:48:24,703 --> 00:48:26,438
- Neat.
- I'm very glad to hear it.

1166
00:48:26,472 --> 00:48:28,507
I only hope it really is
afraid of the light.

1167
00:48:28,540 --> 00:48:30,175
Well, does this mean
we can go to sleep now?

1168
00:48:30,208 --> 00:48:32,310
[All goofy-laugh]

1169
00:48:32,343 --> 00:48:33,578
--Until we've
tested the flares.

1170
00:48:33,612 --> 00:48:35,513
You mean we've gotta
sit up all night?

1171
00:48:35,547 --> 00:48:37,715
Well, after all, we are
the ones nearest to the hill.

1172
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:39,350
We're supposed
to signal immediately

1173
00:48:39,383 --> 00:48:41,052
if we see any sign
of movement here.

1174
00:48:41,085 --> 00:48:43,255
- Yeah.
- Yeah.
- You sleep first.

1175
00:48:43,288 --> 00:48:45,557
And you keep checking
the reports on the radio.

1176
00:48:45,590 --> 00:48:48,093
I'll stand up here and keep
throwing things.

1177
00:48:48,127 --> 00:48:49,628
You get some sleep now,
okay?

1178
00:48:49,662 --> 00:48:51,062
All right. Keep the fire up.

1179
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:53,532
Yes sir, I will.

1180
00:48:53,565 --> 00:48:56,902
Now, I'm just gonna
take my picture here. Yeah.

1181
00:48:56,935 --> 00:48:58,203
- As a memento.
- You get some sleep.

1182
00:48:58,237 --> 00:49:00,005
- Will you be okay?
- Of course I will.

1183
00:49:00,038 --> 00:49:03,175
That symbol on his back is
japanese for "I'm with stupid."

1184
00:49:03,208 --> 00:49:06,745
- Wait.
- [Radio static]

1185
00:49:06,778 --> 00:49:09,347
Oh. That's my favorite
john cage song.

1186
00:49:11,683 --> 00:49:13,485
D'oh, would you--
next time, I lead.

1187
00:49:13,518 --> 00:49:15,187
You're supposed
to watch here.

1188
00:49:15,220 --> 00:49:16,488
I'll get to sleep.

1189
00:49:16,522 --> 00:49:19,825
Yeah, see you later, then.

1190
00:49:19,858 --> 00:49:21,960
Hey, it's a cheese radio.

1191
00:49:21,993 --> 00:49:25,063
No, it's the all orangesicle
station, I think.

1192
00:49:25,097 --> 00:49:27,565
Yep. Check it out.

1193
00:49:32,570 --> 00:49:34,638
- Hmm.
- Oh man.

1194
00:49:34,673 --> 00:49:35,940
I shouldn't've had
that tofu chili.

1195
00:49:35,973 --> 00:49:37,308
Yeaah!

1196
00:49:37,342 --> 00:49:39,277
- Hey, boss!
- "Free bird!"

1197
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:41,312
- "Free bird!"
- Whoo!

1198
00:49:41,347 --> 00:49:43,382
It's coming! Get up!

1199
00:49:43,415 --> 00:49:44,750
What? What? What?...

1200
00:49:44,783 --> 00:49:47,585
What? What?

1201
00:49:47,618 --> 00:49:50,855
Can eiichi come out
and play?

1202
00:49:50,888 --> 00:49:52,657
Fire the signal!

1203
00:49:52,690 --> 00:49:55,927
I'm your wake-up call!

1204
00:49:55,960 --> 00:49:57,695
Yes, we'll be much safer
out here.

1205
00:49:57,728 --> 00:49:59,765
[Gaos screams]

1206
00:50:01,198 --> 00:50:03,502
- [Man mutters]
- Ooh.

1207
00:50:03,535 --> 00:50:05,403
Hey, you might say he's got
a real flare for this.

1208
00:50:05,437 --> 00:50:07,238
[All chuckle]

1209
00:50:10,808 --> 00:50:12,477
- ♪♪ [Servo hums with score]
- --Fire!

1210
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:14,312
- Open fire!
- Open the window first,

1211
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:17,382
then fire!

1212
00:50:20,218 --> 00:50:22,820
Ooh. Boy.

1213
00:50:24,757 --> 00:50:26,892
Grace jones
takes one to the head.

1214
00:50:26,925 --> 00:50:30,562
- Ouch!
- She can't take it there.

1215
00:50:30,595 --> 00:50:34,565
Ha-hah! This is fun!

1216
00:50:34,598 --> 00:50:38,270
Model tanks
aren't working, captain.

1217
00:50:38,303 --> 00:50:41,105
I'm batman.

1218
00:50:42,773 --> 00:50:46,712
Friends, romans, countrymen,
would you let me talk?

1219
00:50:46,745 --> 00:50:50,115
[Joel as lugosi]
I vant to drink your blood.

1220
00:50:51,583 --> 00:50:53,118
Hey, come on, tokyo.
Give me a hug.

1221
00:50:53,152 --> 00:50:54,385
I know you got it in you.

1222
00:50:54,418 --> 00:50:57,688
It's gaos buscaglia
here talking.

1223
00:50:57,722 --> 00:50:59,357
Oh, I love to laugh!

1224
00:50:59,390 --> 00:51:01,158
Long and loud and clear!

1225
00:51:03,495 --> 00:51:05,063
He's doing lap folds.

1226
00:51:05,097 --> 00:51:07,332
Come on, three more.
Give it to me. Come on.

1227
00:51:07,365 --> 00:51:09,233
Feel the burn.
You gotta want it. Go.

1228
00:51:09,267 --> 00:51:12,970
- Ooh.
- Oops.

1229
00:51:13,003 --> 00:51:16,942
Well, that could've
gone better.

1230
00:51:16,975 --> 00:51:19,343
Call me mariah.

1231
00:51:22,513 --> 00:51:24,883
[All rasp-voice]

1232
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:27,118
Can't understand it.

1233
00:51:27,152 --> 00:51:28,687
Whoa, he's air-surfin'.

1234
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:30,388
[All]
Whoo!

1235
00:51:34,358 --> 00:51:35,860
Night on bald mountain.

1236
00:51:35,893 --> 00:51:39,763
♪♪ [Servo hums mussorgsky]

1237
00:51:39,798 --> 00:51:41,900
- It's moving out.
